.\"
.\" SHMCTL(2) - Substrate Native Personality
.\"
.TH SHMCTL 2 "2026-06-29" "Substrate OS" "System Calls"
.SH NAME
shmctl \- System V shared memory control operations
.SH LIBRARY
Standard C library
.RI ( libc ", " \-lc )
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/ipc.h>
.B #include <sys/shm.h>
.PP
.BI "int shmctl(int " shmid ", int " cmd ", struct shmid_ds *" buf ");
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR shmctl ()
performs the control operation
.I cmd
on the System V shared memory segment identified by
.IR shmid .
.PP
The
.I shmid_ds
structure is defined in
.I <sys/shm.h>
as:
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
struct shmid_ds {
    struct ipc_perm shm_perm;   /* ownership and permissions */
    size_t   shm_segsz;         /* size of segment in bytes */
    time_t   shm_atime;         /* last attach time */
    time_t   shm_dtime;         /* last detach time */
    time_t   shm_ctime;         /* last change time */
    pid_t    shm_cpid;          /* pid of creator */
    pid_t    shm_lpid;          /* pid of last shmat(2)/shmdt(2) */
    shmatt_t shm_nattch;        /* number of current attaches */
};
.EE
.in
.PP
Valid values for
.I cmd
are:
.TP
.B IPC_STAT
Copy the
.I shmid_ds
structure of the segment into
.IR buf .
The caller must have read permission.
.TP
.B IPC_SET
Set the
.IR shm_perm.uid ,
.IR shm_perm.gid ,
and the low 9 bits of
.I shm_perm.mode
from
.IR buf .
The caller must be the owner, the creator, or privileged.
.TP
.B IPC_RMID
Mark the segment to be destroyed.  The segment is removed from the key
namespace immediately; its backing pages are freed once the last process
detaches it.  If no process is attached the pages are freed at once.
The caller must be the owner, the creator, or privileged.
.TP
.B SHM_LOCK
Mark the segment as locked in memory.  Substrate never pages out shared
memory backing, so this only sets the advisory
.B SHM_LOCKED
flag reported by
.BR IPC_STAT .
.TP
.B SHM_UNLOCK
Clear the locked flag.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success 0 is returned.  On error \-1 is returned and
.I errno
is set to indicate the error.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EACCES
.B IPC_STAT
was requested but the caller lacks read permission.
.TP
.B EFAULT
.I buf
points outside the accessible address space.
.TP
.B EIDRM
The segment was removed.
.TP
.B EINVAL
.I shmid
is not a valid identifier, or
.I cmd
is not a recognised operation.
.TP
.B EPERM
.B IPC_SET
or
.B IPC_RMID
was requested but the caller is neither the owner, the creator, nor
privileged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR shmget (2),
.BR shmat (2),
.BR shmdt (2)
